  "final_message": "The bug was the one the README describes: `add_tag` used a single list as its default for `tags`. Every call that left `tags` out added to that same list, so tags from one record showed up in the next.\n\nI changed the default to `tags=None` and create a new empty list inside the function when it's `None`. If the caller passes their own list, it is still used and changed directly. `remove_tag` and `test_public.py` are unchanged, and the public test passes.\n\nDONE: Replaced add_tag's mutable default with tags=None plus a fresh list per call, so tags no longer leak between calls; test_public passes.",
