      "final_message": "I rewrote `solution.py` so `semver_compare(a, b)` follows the README contract, and both public tests pass.\n\n- **Input check:** each version must match `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` exactly, using only ASCII digits and no leading zeros. Anything else raises `ValueError`, including strings with a trailing newline. A non-string argument raises `TypeError`.\n- **Comparison:** the three parts are compared as integers, left to right, and the function returns `-1`, `0` or `1`.\n\nI also ran some extra checks of my own. Comparison is numeric, so `1.10.0` counts as newer than `1.9.9`. These inputs were all rejected: two or four parts, `01`-style leading zeros, a trailing newline, a leading space, negative numbers, non-ASCII digits, and `v`/`-rc` prefixes or suffixes.\n\nDONE: Rewrote semver_compare to strictly validate MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (ValueError/TypeError) and compare numerically, returning -1/0/1.",
